Write the following do-while loop in equivalent while-loop form.
```c
void main(void)
{
    int a = 3;
    do
    {
        printf("%d\n", a);
        a = a + 3;
    } while(a <= 10);
}
```

What is the output of the following program statements?
```c
for(int a = 1; a < 5; a++)
{
    for(int b = a; b < 5; b++)
        printf("%d", b);
    printf("\n");
}
```

What will be the output of the following program?
```c
void main()
{
    int n = 5;
    if(n < 6)
        printf("hello");
    if(n == 5)
        printf("hi");
    else
        printf("no");
}
```

Write the equivalent code of the following statement in while-loop form.
```c
for(a = 1; a <= 100; a++)
    printf("%d\n", a);
```

Debug the following program.
```c
(
printf("I am a good programmer");
)
```

Write the output of the following C-program statement.
```c
for(int i = 2; i < 10; i++)
    printf("%d", i);
if(i % 2 == 0)
    continue;
printf("\n");
```
